※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4262
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4262 LANG_MASK_TOO_LONG

※ The widest whole number there is has sixty-four bits, so a mask is of at most
※ sixty-four truth values.  A longer run is several masks, one of each part of
※ it copied out apart.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let c: u8⟦65⟧ = 65 ⍴ 0u8
    if ⎕mask(c = 0u8) = 0u64: 1u6 else: 0u6
